  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Among given aliphatic amines, 2&deg; amine is most basic, followed by 3&deg; amine and 1&deg; amine.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0061_062f564693ff.png\" style=\"width: 782px; height: 153px;\" />Therefore, the correct basic strength (K<sub>b</sub>) order of the given amines is</p><p>(C)&nbsp;&gt; (D) &gt; (B) &gt; (A)</p><p>The pK<sub>b</sub> order of the given amines will be just the opposite of their basic strength order.</p><p>The order is (A) &gt; (B) &gt; (D) &gt; (C)</p><p>So the correct answer is A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
